DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Vector");
BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 10, -4, -4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -1, -4, 1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -1, -10, 6 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-1, -4, 1>") x Compute("<-1, -10, 6>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<10, -4, -4>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{w} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-1, -10, 6>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-1, -4, 1>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -6, 0, 9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 6, 1, 10 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<6, 1, 10>") x Compute("<-6, 0, 9>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<6, 1, 10>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<6, 1, 10>") x Compute("<-6, 0, 9>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-6, 0, 9>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -5, -4, -10 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -3, -3, -4 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-3, -3, -4>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-5, -4, -10>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-5, -4, -10>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-3, -3, -4>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -8, 0, -9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 7, 7, 0 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 5, 6, -8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<5, 6, -8>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{w} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<5, 6, -8>"))}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<5, 6, -8>") . Compute("<7, 7, 0>")}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<5, 6, -8>") x Compute("<7, 7, 0>")}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<5, 6, -8>") x Compute("<-8, 0, -9>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<7, 7, 0>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 2, -4, -9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 6, -3, -9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 2, -8, -5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<6, -3, -9>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<6, -3, -9>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<2, -4, -9>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<2, -8, -5>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<2, -4, -9>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
